METHOD
For each deterministic arbitrary reduced-factor word, the audit
constructs the exact unperiodized triangular convolution and its
ordinary square profile m.  At every active affine wall nL it computes
the K+1 margin coordinates of the complete suffix D_n, then tries
every admissible next reduced factor q.

For every output row r it independently convolves the line profile
by tau_q and verifies the exact generator identity

  u_(n,r)(m chi_q^2)
   =sum_s T_(r,s)u_(n,s)(m)
     +sum_(t=nL-2q+r)^(nL+2q-r-1)m_t,

where the last sum is present only for r<2q and
T=B(N_q^(K))^2C is the finite transform in margin coordinates.
It also discards every positive T coefficient and checks that the
remaining consecutive wall block pays all negative T entries.

All 1,238,541 identities agree exactly, and all 1,238,541 stronger
payments are nonnegative.  These zero failures are bounded evidence
for the all-wall global-payment target, not an unbounded proof.
The separate length-100 stress adds 199,616 exact identities and
payments without a failure.

